# Development Guidelines

## About Design Documents

`docs/ja/` is the source of truth. `docs/en/` does not exist yet.

### Architecture & Design

- `docs/ja/develop/design/architecture.md` - Overall architecture
- `docs/ja/develop/design/tech-stack.md` - Tech stack and crate layout
- `docs/ja/develop/design/ui/` - Slint UI design
  - `layers.md` - Layer responsibilities and dependency rules
  - `slint-patterns.md` - Slint design patterns
  - `viewmodel-architecture.md` - ViewModel layer
  - `responsive-layout.md` - Breakpoints and touch requirements
  - `core-bridge.md` - How the UI talks to the core
  - `i18n-system.md` - Internationalization
- `docs/ja/develop/design/platform/platform-abstraction.md` - OS abstraction
- `docs/ja/develop/design/backend/` - Rust design
  - `rust-guidelines.md` - Clean architecture, error handling, async
  - `transaction-management.md` - Transaction boundaries
- `docs/ja/develop/design/data/` - Data-related design
  - `data-model.md` - Data structure specifications
  - `data-security.md` - Security design
  - `automerge-repo-dataflow.md` - Data flow design
  - `partial-update-implementation.md` - Partial update system
  - `entity/` - Entity definitions

### Development Rules

- `docs/ja/develop/rules/` - coding rules (ui.md, backend.md, testing.md, etc.)

### Requirements Definition

- `docs/ja/develop/requirements/` - performance.md, accessibility.md, testing.md, etc.

### Testing

- `docs/ja/develop/design/testing.md` - Testing strategy and guidelines

Refer to these documents as needed and work based on the latest design information.

